# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ----------------------------------------------------------------
# the generator's rocks that floated over the slope, and walls left wholly under the ground (ground check, 2026-10-23)
clear at 12.85 12.01 r=1.5 only=SmallRock
# (and the generator's things under the warden's post, which kept its floor's posts out and left its roof unheld)
clear at 31.3 -9.5 r=3

info title=Hadal Commons
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A city cut into the trench wall 45 m down: stone houses with lit windows, air in four of them, a caged diver, and great doors sealed under the Ringwave. The eighth island of The Sunken Kingdom.
island on.arrive=message||A buoy over black water. Far, far below: a few small, warm windows.

story cagekey|Cage key|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|The key to the cage in house 3, from the broadcast room.

note minutes Commons council minutes | COMMONS COUNCIL - LAST MINUTES (taken by G. Fennick, door warden, because nobody else would)\n\n1. Air holds in houses 1, 2, 3 and the cellar.\n2. The long shadow was seen at the doors again. Motion: the doors stay shut. Carried.\n3. The Spire sent the lift for the twelve shuttle children ONLY. Motion: we send them. Carried, with shouting. Warden Fennick to ride up with them, since he is "expendable and annoying". Accepted.\n4. Spire control room code changed to 2817. Do not write it down. (Noted: it is written down.)\n5. The diver, Marlowe, says the Spire drowned the stations on purpose. Motion: we do not believe her. Not carried. Not anything. We just sat there.\n6. The Director asks that Marlowe be kept below. Fennick says he will see to it, and looks at his boots.
note broadcast The last broadcast | THE LAST BROADCAST (transcript)\n\nThis is Hadal Commons. The doors are shut. Repeat, the doors are shut.\nThe children have gone up in the Spire's lift. All twelve. The warden went with them, complaining.\nWhoever finds this: the Spire can open the Network again - or seal the Hollow for good. Somebody has to go up and choose, because the man up there has been choosing for all of us.\nP.S. from the warden: The cage key is under the radio. I am a door warden, not a jailer, and I am very sorry, Ines. Orders. You know whose.
note inesaccount Ines Marlowe's account | INES MARLOWE - WRITTEN IN THE CAGE, ON THE BACK OF A MENU\n\nYou have Mo. You actually have Mo. I knitted that whale on the roofs in the winter Milo had measles, and he has not slept without it since.\nMilo is safe. Fennick took them up the lift to the Spire; the Director let the children go. The rest of us he kept below in the dark, with the doors shut, because the dark is quiet and the quiet keeps the Stalker in the Hollow.\nThat was his plan. Drown the lit stations, cut the cables, keep the Commons dark - and leave one light burning far away, on the roofs, for it to swim to instead of us. The beacon you answered.\nGo up to the Spire. RESTORE the Network or SEAL the Hollow. I can't choose for you. I would only choose Milo.
note toolmaker Toolmaker's chest | The toolmaker's chest: titanium tool plans.
note packchest Broadcast room chest | Advanced backpack plans, and a key under the radio.
note inesbag Ines's bag | Ines's diving bag: her spare tank and a photo of Milo.
note wardenchest Door warden's chest | Fennick's chest: electric zipline tool plans, "for the Spire".
loot toolmaker Blueprint_TitaniumTools*1;TitaniumOre*1
prop toolmaker loot.refill=0
loot packchest Blueprint_BackpackAdvanced*1;story:cagekey*1;Leather*2
prop packchest loot.refill=0
loot inesbag Rope*2;Leather*1
prop inesbag loot.refill=0
prop inesbag obj.name=inesbag
prop inesbag if.open=signal|inesfree
prop inesbag else.open=message||Ines's bag is inside the cage with her.
loot wardenchest Blueprint_ZiplineToolElectric*1;Bolt*2
prop wardenchest loot.refill=0

prop plazazone zone.id=plaza
prop plazazone zone.radius=5
prop plazazone zone.message=Hadal Commons. The bell's landing, the plaza - and lit windows up the trench wall.
prop inescage obj.name=inescage
prop inescage survivor.name=Ines Marlowe
prop inescage survivor.id=sunken_ines
prop inescage survivor.key=cagekey
prop inescage survivor.signal=inesfree
prop inescage survivor.line=You found the key. I'm Ines Marlowe. Is that - is that Mo? Milo's safe, he went up. Get to the Spire. And don't open those doors.
prop doorszone zone.id=doors
prop doorszone zone.radius=4
prop doorszone zone.repeat=never
prop doorszone zone.message=The great doors. Over them, painted in rust red: a ring, three waves across it.
prop doorszone on.enter=camera|doorcam|greatdoors|6|40
prop doorcam obj.name=doorcam
prop greatdoors obj.name=greatdoors
prop darkcity atmo.fog=#06141c
prop darkcity atmo.fogAmount=0.65
prop darkcity atmo.light=#2a4a5a
prop darkcity atmo.lightAmount=0.25
prop darkcity zone.radius=40

note hc_cavechest Quarry chest | A quarryman's chest: chisels gone to rust, and titanium chips he kept.
loot hc_cavechest TitaniumOre*2;Rope*2;Bolt*2;Copper*1
prop hc_cavechest loot.refill=0
note hc_ruinnote Warden's lodge note | WARDEN'S LODGE - G. FENNICK\n\nSpare tanks are in the cage by the lodge. The cage key went with Ines. If you have bolt cutters, take what you need, and close the lid after, I am not your mother.\nThe lever for the great doors is on the post by my lodge. Behind them is the strongroom of the Commons, which holds everything the council saved for the day the Spire answered. It has not answered.\nIf you are the Stalker, go home. I have said this on every door in the Network now, and you have not gone home once. I am beginning to think you cannot read.
note hc_wrecknote Wagon driver's chit | WAGON DRIVER'S CHIT\n\nTwo wagons of quarry stone, Commons terrace 3. Signed, N. Abara.\nThe rails ran out at the trench floor. So did I.\nOn the back: I was hauling stone when the lights went out across the whole Commons at once. Not a fault. A switch. Somebody flicked us off from up the trench like a bedroom light.\nThen it got very quiet. And in the quiet, from the Hollow under the lip, something started to sing the lift's bell back at us. Ding. Ding. Calling.
note hc_wreckcrate Wagon load | The wagon's load box: cut stone and what the quarrymen dropped.
loot hc_wreckcrate Stone*6;TitaniumOre*1;Scrap*2;Rope*1
prop hc_wreckcrate loot.refill=0
prop wardencage obj.name=wardencage
prop wardencage on.use=message||The chain snaps and the cage swings open.\nhide|wardencage\nsignal||wardencage
note lodgechest Warden's store | The warden's store, safe in its cage: spare tanks and titanium.
loot lodgechest OxygenBottle*1;TitaniumIngot*2;Bolt*3
prop lodgechest loot.refill=0
prop lodgechest if.open=signal|wardencage
prop lodgechest else.open=message||The chest is inside the chained cage.
note trenchchest Trench box | A box dropped down the dark trench: copper and a battery, dry in wax.
loot trenchchest Copper*3;Battery*1;CircuitBoard*1
prop trenchchest loot.refill=0
prop hctrenchdark zone.radius=9
prop hctrenchdark zone.hazard=dark
prop hctrenchdark zone.hazardMsg=The trench swallows the light. A headlight would show the way.
prop doorlever obj.name=doorlever
prop doorlever beh.use=Pull the great doors' lever
prop doorlever on.use=sound||event:/exploring/obstacles/keypad/keypad_correct\nsignal||hc_doors\nmessage||Far off, across the Commons, something heavy unlocks.
note strongroom Commons strongroom | The Commons' strongroom behind the great doors: what the council saved for the day the Spire answered.
loot strongroom TitaniumIngot*2;OxygenBottle*1;CircuitBoard*1;Battery*2
prop strongroom loot.refill=0
prop greatdoors if.use=signal|hc_doors
prop greatdoors else.use=message||Locked. The door warden worked them from a lever by his lodge.
# --- DEEP 1-HOUR (10-24): story items, notes and checks
story hc_key|Scavenger's key|Hinge|The scavenger's key, from the chest at the bottom of his hideout.
story sk_crest|Kingdom crest shard|Bolt|A shard of the Sunken Kingdom's crest, from a drowned building. The Hollow's crown vault wants nine.
note hcdeep Scavenger's strongbox | The scavenger's strongbox: his best loot and a crest shard.
loot hcdeep story:sk_crest*1;TradeToken*2;TitaniumOre*2;Bolt*3;OxygenBottle*1
prop hcdeep loot.refill=0
note hclocker Spire locker | The scavenger's locker on his spire: Commons brass.
loot hclocker TitaniumIngot*2;MetalIngot*3;CopperIngot*2;Battery*1
prop hclocker loot.refill=0
note hcsumnote Scavenger's boast | TOP OF THE SPIRE\n\nNobody climbs up here. Nobody gets past my wires either.\nIf you did both, the locker is yours; I have a better one. From up here you can see the Commons - the lit windows of houses 1, 2 and 3, the dark everywhere else - and above it all the Spire, perched on the trench lip like a heron.
note hcbldnote Scavenger's inventory | WHAT I TOOK - AND WHAT I SAW\n\nWindows, wire, the Commons' brass, one crown shard. Take the shard. You've earned it, swimming through my wires.\nWhat I saw, from the top of my spire, the night the stations went dark: lights going out one by one across the sea - the labs, the domes, the Yard - and in the middle of it all, the Spire on the trench, every window lit, and a man at the top window watching.\nHe watched every one go. Then he picked up his radio and said sorry to each of them.\nGo up the trench to the Sealkeeper Spire. Tell him the scavenger saw.
note hcledge Scavenger's stash | One of the scavenger's stashes, on the spire's shelf.
loot hcledge Rope*3;Bolt*2;Feather*3
prop hcledge loot.refill=0
note hccave2chest Warden's spare chest | A warden's spare chest in the rock cave.
loot hccave2chest CopperOre*3;Rope*2;Battery*1
prop hccave2chest loot.refill=0
prop hcsummit zone.id=hc_summit
prop hcsummit zone.radius=2.5
prop hcsummit zone.message=Out of the water at the top of the trench spire. 47 m of rock below you.
note hcnote1 Scavenger's note I | NOTE I - THE SCAVENGER\n\nYou followed me out here. Bold. The first wire is low, so swim high over the flat stones, unless you want to be a pincushion.\nI took what the Commons would not use. Windows. Wire. The council's brass. Stealing from people who have given up is not stealing, it is tidying.
note hcnote2 Scavenger's note II | NOTE II\n\nThe second wire is across the gap. Go round by the left.\nI saw the lift go up with the children. I saw the warden hold the smallest one's hand the whole way. I did not steal anything that night. I am not a monster. I am a professional.
note hcnote3 Scavenger's note III | NOTE III\n\nThe last one is at the door. Wait for the spikes to drop, then go.\nBelow the hideout the store is drowned. I keep the good things at the bottom, and the crown shard I lifted from the old king's arch, because one day somebody will need nine of them, and I will charge them a great deal.
prop hctrip1 obj.name=hctrip1
